<BlogPost slug="iptv-free-trial-checklist">
  <p>A free trial only helps if you test the things that decide whether a service will work for <em>you</em>. A 24-hour trial passes quickly, so plan it before you start. This checklist works for any IPTV service, and it is what we suggest for the <a href="/free-trial/">Prime IPTV 24-hour free trial</a>, which needs no credit card.</p>

  <h2>Before you request a trial</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Pick the device you will actually use.</strong> Test on the TV or box you would watch on every day, not a spare phone.</li>
    <li><strong>Install a player in advance.</strong> This saves trial hours. See the <a href="/setup/">device guides</a> and <a href="/blog/best-iptv-players/">player comparison</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Write down your must-haves:</strong> the five channels, the two sports and the handful of movies or series you would hate to lose.</li>
    <li><strong>Note your internet speed.</strong> A quick speed test at the time you plan to watch gives you a baseline.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>The 24-hour test plan</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>What to check</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>1. Login</strong></td><td>Add the login in your player and confirm channels load without errors.</td><td>If setup is hard, daily use will be too.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>2. Your channels</strong></td><td>Find every item on your must-have list.</td><td>Channel count matters less than whether <em>your</em> channels are there.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>3. Peak time</strong></td><td>Watch a busy evening slot or a live sports event.</td><td>Problems usually show at peak hours, not at 10 a.m.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>4. Picture quality</strong></td><td>Try an HD or FHD channel and, if your TV supports it, a 4K one.</td><td>Confirms the quality your device and connection can really use.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>5. Channel switching</strong></td><td>Flip between channels and across categories.</td><td>Slow zapping becomes annoying quickly.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>6. TV guide (EPG)</strong></td><td>Check that the guide loads, shows now/next and matches the channels.</td><td>A missing or wrong guide is a daily irritation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>7. On-demand library</strong></td><td>Search for several movies and series you care about.</td><td>The library only helps if it has what you watch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>8. Support</strong></td><td>Send a real question by WhatsApp or email and note how quickly and clearly it is answered.</td><td>Support quality matters most when something breaks.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>9. Multiple screens</strong></td><td>If you plan to use more than one screen, test two at once.</td><td>Confirms your connection handles the load. See <a href="/blog/how-many-iptv-connections-do-i-need/">how many connections you need</a>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Questions to ask any IPTV provider</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Is there a refund policy, and how long does it last? (Prime IPTV: 7-day money-back guarantee. See the <a href="/refund/">refund policy</a>.)</li>
    <li>Is there a contract or a cancellation fee? (Prime IPTV: no contract; cancellation available.)</li>
    <li>How many simultaneous connections does each plan include?</li>
    <li>How will I receive my login and how quickly after payment? (Prime IPTV: by WhatsApp or email, normally within minutes.)</li>
    <li>What payment methods are accepted, and is the price clear before you pay?</li>
    <li>How do I contact support, and when is it available? (Prime IPTV: 24/7.)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to do if something does not work</h2>
  <p>Do not write off a service in the first five minutes. Work through our <a href="/blog/iptv-buffering-troubleshooting/">buffering and login checklist</a> first, because many trial problems come from the player, the Wi-Fi or a typo in the login rather than the service. If it still fails, tell support exactly which device, player, channel and time, so they can help.</p>

  <h2>Deciding after the trial</h2>
  <p>Decide using your list rather than the first impression: did your must-have channels work, did peak-time viewing hold up, did support answer clearly? If yes, compare the <a href="/pricing/">plans</a>, and remember that the money-back guarantee gives you a further 7 days after you subscribe.</p>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Ready to test?</strong> <a href="/free-trial/">Request your 24-hour Prime IPTV free trial</a>. No credit card required.</p></div>

  <h2>Quick answers</h2>
  <h3>Do I need a credit card for the Prime IPTV trial?</h3>
  <p>No. The 24-hour free trial does not require a credit card.</p>
  <h3>How long is the trial?</h3>
  <p>24 hours.</p>
  <h3>Can I test 4K during the trial?</h3>
  <p>Yes, if your TV, player and connection support 4K. A wired connection works best.</p>
  <h3>What if I run out of time?</h3>
  <p>Plan your tests before you start and install the player first. If you still need more time, tell support what you could not test.</p>
</BlogPost>
